In the following, we evaluate $\chi_{(n)}(G)$ for a few special graph families. See Section \ref{sec:4} for the corresponding results on~$\chi_{n}(G)$.

\begin{theorem}
    Let $n,m\in\Z^+$ with $n,m\geq 2$. For the complete graph,
    $$\chi_{(n)}(K_m) =
    \begin{cases}
        m, &\text{if } n > 2 \text{ or } n=2 \text{ with } 2\mid m, \\
        \text{does not exist}, &\text{otherwise}.
    \end{cases}
    $$
\end{theorem}

