The retained module passes G1–G8 locally and fails only the pending G9 oracle requirement, exactly as expected for a rejected build. I corrected the paper’s theorem numbering, renamed the module so it cannot be mistaken for a shippable generator, and wrote the rejection with the measured algorithm/shortcut costs and every scored oracle result.
The family fails H on Track B, so shipping and G9 arms are inapplicable. The built module and official transcript are retained, and the rejection is documented with measured costs and scored oracle outcomes.
